# 18-COG / COGS and supplier

**Goes here.** Cutting landed cost on something you already sell, and running the
supplier relationship. BOM and should cost, supplier discovery and vetting, MOQ and
price breaks, incoterms and landed cost, negotiation levers, quality control, dual
sourcing, sourcing from overseas manufacturers.

## Not here

- Finding a supplier for a product that does not exist yet -> 01-PRD
- How the purchase order gets financed -> 20-FIN
- Which costs count as COGS for accounting -> 20-FIN and 06-MEA
- 3PL and warehouse negotiation -> 21-OPS

COG negotiates the supplier. OPS negotiates the 3PL. FIN finances the order and
decides how the cost is booked.

